# Copy to .env (loaded automatically by the justfile via `set dotenv-load := true`).
# Every var below maps 1:1 to a `configmanbearpig.py` CLI flag — the comment
# alongside lists the equivalent flag on `uv run openhound collect sccm`.
#
# Precedence (highest wins): CLI flag > env var (this file or shell) > default.

# ===== Connection ============================================================
SOURCES__SCCM__DOMAIN=mayyhem.com                      # -d / --domain
SOURCES__SCCM__DOMAIN_CONTROLLER=dc.mayyhem.com        # -dc / --domain-controller
SOURCES__SCCM__USERNAME=MAYYHEM\domainadmin            # -u / --username
SOURCES__SCCM__PASSWORD=password                       # -p / --password
# LDAP transport (LDAPS / StartTLS / plain) and hardening (NTLM signing,
# channel binding) are auto-detected at bind time — no knobs to set. The
# walk tries LDAPS:636+CBT → StartTLS:389+CBT → LDAP:389+NTLM sign/seal and
# stops the chain on credential-class failures so it never racks up
# badPwdCount across attempts. Pin --ldap-port if 636/389 aren't right.
# SOURCES__SCCM__LDAP_PORT=389                         # --ldap-port (omit to auto-detect)

# ===== Collection ============================================================
# Comma-separated method list. "All" (the default) runs every phase. Use a
# subset like "LDAP,SMB,WMI" to skip the others (replaces the OH-specific
# OPENHOUND_SCCM_DISABLE_* env vars from earlier releases).
# SOURCES__SCCM__COLLECTION_METHODS=All                # -m / --collection-methods
# SOURCES__SCCM__COMPUTERS=ps1-mp.mayyhem.com,ps1-db.mayyhem.com  # -c / --computers
# SOURCES__SCCM__COMPUTER_FILE=./targets.txt           # -cf / --computer-file
# SOURCES__SCCM__SMS_PROVIDER=ps1-psv.mayyhem.com      # -sms / --sms-provider
# SOURCES__SCCM__SITE_CODES=PS1,CAS                    # -sc / --site-codes (DNS phase)

# ===== Behaviour flags =======================================================
# SOURCES__SCCM__DISABLE_POSSIBLE_EDGES=false          # --disable-possible-edges
# SOURCES__SCCM__ENABLE_BAD_OPSEC=false                # --enable-bad-opsec (NAA decryption, etc.)
# SOURCES__SCCM__THREADS=1                             # -t / --threads (per-host phase parallelism; sequential today)
# SOURCES__SCCM__SHOW_CLEARTEXT_PASSWORDS=false        # --show-cleartext-passwords

# ===== Machine Account / CRED-2 ==============================================
# These flags are accepted today but the CRED-2 SCCM-client-registration →
# policy-request → NAA decryption chain is not yet implemented in OpenHound.
# Setting them has no observable effect until that chain lands.
# SOURCES__SCCM__MACHINE_NAME=MAYYHEM\OPENHOUND01$     # --machine-name
# SOURCES__SCCM__MACHINE_PASS=...                      # --machine-pass
# SOURCES__SCCM__CLIENT_NAME=openhound01.mayyhem.com   # --client-name
# SOURCES__SCCM__CREATE_MACHINE_ACCOUNT=auto           # --create-machine-account
# SOURCES__SCCM__USE_ALTAUTH=false                     # --use-altauth
# SOURCES__SCCM__REGISTRATION_SLEEP=10                 # --registration-sleep

# ===== Network ===============================================================
# SOURCES__SCCM__SOCKS_PROXY=127.0.0.1:1080            # --socks-proxy (DHCP / TFTP path)
